        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Camlaren Mine, Barton Mine, Net Lake Mine, Northeastern Ontario, Canada\n- Topics: World War II, mine development, mine fire, abandoned mines\n\nFacts:\n- Conditions attributed to World War II halted development at Camlaren Mine in 1939.\n- Barton Mine, also known as Net Lake Mine, is an abandoned surface and underground mine in Northeastern Ontario, Canada.\n- Barton Mine was the site of a fire in the early 1900s, after which it never had active mining again.",
